        "title": "fix(auto-reply): stop treating wait as abort trigger",
        "body": "## Summary\n- remove `wait` from natural-language abort triggers\n- add regression coverage so `wait` / `please wait` no longer count as abort requests while explicit stop commands still do\n\n## Why\nIn Telegram upstream coordination groups, `wait` is a normal operational reply. Treating it as an abort command can cause OpenClaw to reply `⚙️ Agent was aborted.` and skip normal upstream handling.\n\n## Test\n- `pnpm exec vitest run src/auto-reply/reply/abort.test.ts --config test/vitest/vitest.config.ts`",
